Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 06:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] gallium/u_screen: query DRM_CAP_PRIME on Phoenix-RTOS too

u_init_pipe_screen_caps() fills caps.dmabuf from drmGetCap(DRM_CAP_PRIME)
only on Linux, the BSDs and managarm. On Phoenix-RTOS (libdrm-phoenix) the
query was compiled out, so every screen reported caps.dmabuf = 0, and with it:

- gbm_dri: has_dmabuf_export = false, so gbm_dri_bo_create() allocated every
  GBM surface buffer as a dumb buffer without a DRI image; the EGL GBM
  platform then handed that NULL image to dri2_allocate_textures() (a NULL
  dereference at the first eglMakeCurrent -- kmscube, first Pi run);
- dri_screen: dmabuf_import/has_dmabuf = false;
- EGL: no EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import(_modifiers)/EGL_MESA_image_dma_buf_export.

libdrm-phoenix answers DRM_CAP_PRIME (IMPORT | EXPORT on the v3d render node),
so the generic query is correct here as it is on the other DRM systems.
---
 src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_screen.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_screen.c b/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_screen.c
index da9cdfcec5c..5aa33fb317e 100644
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_screen.c
@@ -132,7 +132,8 @@ u_init_pipe_screen_caps(struct pipe_screen *pscreen, int accel)
 
    caps->throttle = true;
 
-#if defined(HAVE_LIBDRM) && (DETECT_OS_LINUX || DETECT_OS_BSD || DETECT_OS_MANAGARM)
+#if defined(HAVE_LIBDRM) && (DETECT_OS_LINUX || DETECT_OS_BSD || DETECT_OS_MANAGARM || \
+                             DETECT_OS_PHOENIX)
    if (pscreen->get_screen_fd) {
       uint64_t cap;
       int fd = pscreen->get_screen_fd(pscreen);
